# Line endings, for everyone and every computer working on this repo.
#
# Git stores text files with LF ("\n") line endings and checks them out with LF too, on Windows
# as well. Modern editors (VS Code included) handle LF fine, and it stops the
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warnings on every commit.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows scripts keep Windows line endings (CRLF), or cmd.exe can misread them.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary files: never touch them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.jar binary
